%I A402603 #9 Nov 27 2026 08:59:46
%S A402603 3,2,6,0,4,6,1
%N A402603 Decimal expansion of the sum of reciprocals of the Zuckerman numbers.
%C A402603 The Zuckerman numbers (A007602) are zeroless and form a subsequence of the zeroless numbers (A052382). Therefore, Sum_{n>=1} 1/A007602(n) < Sum_{n>=1} 1/A052382(n) = 23.1034479..., where 23.1034479... is the Kempner series (A082839). Consequently, the sum of the reciprocals of the Zuckerman numbers converges, and the decimal expansion of this sum is considered here.
%C A402603 This constant was first explicitly recorded in the OEIS by _Amiram Eldar_ in the Formula section of A335037.
%F A402603 Equals Sum_{k>=1} 1/A007602(k).
%F A402603 Equals lim_{m->oo} (1/m) * Sum_{k=1..m} A335037(k).
%e A402603 3.260461...
%Y A402603 Cf. A007602, A335037, A052382, A082839.
%K A402603 cons,nonn,more,new
%O A402603 1,1
%A A402603 _Bernard Schott_, Nov 21 2026
